[{:db/id 17592186124486 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58" :question/id #uuid "0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58" :question/math-academy-id "q-35759" :question/problem "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." :question/worked-solution "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & -5{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4{x}_{2} \\\\ 20{x}_{2} & -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} & 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 20 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -12 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 15 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are  the $1$st,  $2$nd and $3$rd. Therefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 10{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nConsequently, ${A,B,C}$ is linearly independent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" :answer-field/choices ["answer-561c2f0d-be65-5b74-80cb-c4d610f62978" "answer-37daef1d-9729-5a8c-96e9-3c9478596dc7" "answer-7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" "answer-7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" "answer-19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-561c2f0d-be65-5b74-80cb-c4d610f62978" :answer/id #uuid "561c2f0d-be65-5b74-80cb-c4d610f62978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37daef1d-9729-5a8c-96e9-3c9478596dc7" :answer/id #uuid "37daef1d-9729-5a8c-96e9-3c9478596dc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" :answer/id #uuid "7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" :answer/id #uuid "7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" :answer/id #uuid "19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The set is linearly independent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-86f80e75-0963-5bd9-910a-02c8b66996e2" :activity/id #uuid "86f80e75-0963-5bd9-910a-02c8b66996e2" :activity/title "Linear Independence in Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048257 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-a04781cc-ebc3-5bc2-92d1-20e2247f29f6" "step-91898925-eff3-5fa3-8a62-f041326f9f41" "step-13861d32-2afe-51b5-bbef-cdba909877c7" "step-26514834-a2cf-541c-940e-f1a92276ce78" "step-9a3eaaac-6a96-5a5c-a458-0780e627e72a"] :activity/first-step "step-a04781cc-ebc3-5bc2-92d1-20e2247f29f6" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a04781cc-ebc3-5bc2-92d1-20e2247f29f6" :step/id #uuid "a04781cc-ebc3-5bc2-92d1-20e2247f29f6" :step/content 17592186415061 :step/next "step-91898925-eff3-5fa3-8a62-f041326f9f41" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-91898925-eff3-5fa3-8a62-f041326f9f41" :step/id #uuid "91898925-eff3-5fa3-8a62-f041326f9f41" :step/content "question-0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58" :step/next "step-13861d32-2afe-51b5-bbef-cdba909877c7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-13861d32-2afe-51b5-bbef-cdba909877c7" :step/id #uuid "13861d32-2afe-51b5-bbef-cdba909877c7" :step/content 17592186360491 :step/next "step-265148